The safe Rust BCH implementation replaces an earlier AFF3CT-derived C++ adapter.
Algorithm provenance includes AFF3CT revision
0e8ecda8191cec97a6fe86a56de0d957b63b3b04, under the MIT license.
Its full notice is crates/fec-codec/LICENSE-MIT. The Rust implementation uses
bounded Berlekamp-Massey/Chien processing, MSB-first wire order and post-correction
syndrome verification. No AFF3CT binary or C++ runtime is used. Retain that license with any
binary distribution. See docs/reference/coding-mode.md for parameter evidence.
